Q: lodash Mongoose object id difference A: <p>The <strong>_.isEmpty()</strong> function from lodash returns true if the provided value is considered &quot;empty&quot;. For an ObjectID, even if it's not null or undefined, it might still be considered &quot;empty&quot; if lodash's internal logic doesn't recognize it.</p>
<p>In such cases, you might want to check specifically for null or undefined as follows:</p>
<pre><code>if (ObjectId === null || ObjectId === undefined) {
// branchData._id is null or undefined
}
</code></pre>
<p>instead of</p>
<pre><code>   if (_.isEmpty(ObjectId)){

   }
</code></pre>

Q: DO-WHILE loop challenge A: <p>I have added a counter to keep track of the attempts and updated the do-while loop's condition to include this check.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>using static System.Console;

string? actualPassword = &quot;ludo5656&quot;;
string? password;
int attempts = 0;
int maxAttempts = 3;

do
{
    Write(&quot;Enter your password: &quot;);
    password = ReadLine();
    attempts++; // Increment the attempt counter

    if (password != actualPassword)
    {
        WriteLine($&quot;Wrong password. You have {maxAttempts - attempts} attempts remaining.&quot;);
    }
}
// Continue the loop if the password is wrong AND the attempts are less than the maximum allowed
while (password != actualPassword &amp;&amp; attempts &lt; maxAttempts);

// Check the result after the loop ends
if (password == actualPassword)
{
    WriteLine(&quot;Correct!&quot;);
}
else
{
    WriteLine(&quot;You have reached the maximum number of attempts. Access denied.&quot;);
}
</code></pre>
