<thead>
<tr>
<th>Change</th>
<th>Purpose</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>int attempts = 0;</code></td>
<td>Initializes a variable to count the number of attempts the user has made.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>attempts++;</code></td>
<td>With each loop execution, the counter is incremented by one.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&amp;&amp; attempts &lt; maxAttempts</code></td>
<td>Adds a second condition to the while statement. The loop now stops if the password is correct OR if the number of attempts has reached the maximum limit (3).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Final <code>if/else</code> block</td>
<td>After the loop has finished, this block checks whether the last entered password was correct to decide which message to display: success or an error for too many attempts.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
